    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Though framed in a narrative arc, this podcast includes an academic look at three major elements all circling the main themes of skepticism and belief. First, we delve into the phenomenon of extraterrestrials - are they out there or perhaps already here? - looking at both the physical science and cultural elements. Then, we get into Spiritualism and the paranormal, talking about ghosts in connection with the Stanford family, addressing how Spiritualism can be both a science and a religion, and looking at the reasons people want to believe in ghosts. We end with a discussion of conspiracy theories, from autism and vaccination to Bigfoot. Here the big question is what positive purposes conspiracy theorists might serve in society but also the role skepticism needs to play. Taken together, these three segments form a comprehensive look at the stranger side of belief.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
